  "id": "pop_minang",
  "name": "Pop Minang (Minangkabau-language pop)",
  "family": "pop",
  "lineage": "Popular song in the Minangkabau language that grew from post-independence Minang orchestras in Jakarta and Padang into a large regional cassette and later VCD industry centred on Padang. Arrangements set Minang verse over a pop band of guitar, bass, drums and keyboard, often adding the colour of talempong kettle gongs (the canang card stands in) and the saluang bamboo flute (the generic bamboo-flute card stands in).",
